    "body": "## Overview\nCancel a finished or aborted Mooncake Store request's queued lookup in its finish callback, before the next scheduler metadata batch.\n\n## Claims\n- Both finish APIs reuse the existing idempotent `discard()` operation.\n- Already-running RPCs are not interrupted. No TTFT or throughput gain is claimed.\n\n## Validation\nHead `fdd78debf`, base `d0d681e40`. Existing connector/scheduler CPU suites: **113 passed**; whole-diff pre-commit, including mypy, passed. A separate cancellation probe passed for both finish APIs; replacing cleanup with the old no-op makes both probes fail because two RPCs are issued instead of one. Events control the external reply; the lookup executor is real. The probe is external validation, not a committed CI regression.\n\n```bash\nHF_HUB_OFFLINE=1 VLLM_TARGET_DEVICE=cpu CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' \\\nuv run --no-project .venv/bin/python -m pytest -q \\\n  tests/v1/kv_connector/unit/test_mooncake_store_connector.py \\\n  tests/v1/kv_connector/unit/test_mooncake_store_scheduler.py\n```\n\nEarlier native Mooncake + OPT-125M checks returned identical tokens and top-5 logprobs for base/patch/reference, including misses, remote hits and reset; not rerun this round. Local validation does not mean upstream CI passed.\n\n## Details\n`request_finished()` delegates to `request_finished_all_groups()`, so one cleanup site covers both APIs. The standalone PR is limited to two production lines; the added test and its dedicated CI step have been removed. This independent finish cleanup complements #61292's input-thread prefetch; #50464 concerns teardown. AI assistance was used for implementation and validation.\n\n---\n<details>\n<summary>Pull Request Checklist</summary>\n\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill.\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n- [x] Design Fit\n- [x] Testing and Validation (scope and gaps above)\n- [x] Code Quality and Style\n- [x] Pull Request Contents\n\n</details>\n",
